# Live config.  May contain notification credentials (Pushover token and user
# key), so it must never be committed.  Only the .example file belongs in the
# repository.
#
# The second pattern covers the realistic accident: a live config saved under a
# variant name such as tailscale_watchdog.conf.bak or .conf.local while editing
# on the router.  The negation keeps the example file tracked.
tailscale_watchdog.conf
tailscale_watchdog.conf.*
!tailscale_watchdog.conf.example

# Merge and patch leftovers.  These can contain a full copy of whatever they
# were derived from, including a live config.
*.orig
*.rej

# Environment files that may carry provider credentials
.env
.env.*

# Assistant and tooling logs
.codex-log
*.log

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
